---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const PAGE_URL = 'https://ka-performancefl.com/services/ai-integration/';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What would an AI assistant actually do on our site?',
    a: 'The proven win is answering the questions your team answers forty times a week, at whatever hour the visitor turns up, then handing over a qualified lead with the details already collected. After that it is usually intake, quoting, triage, or search. If your team is retyping the same answer, that is the job.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will it make things up about my business?',
    a: 'That is the risk we spend the most time on. Assistants we build run on a written knowledge base about your business, are told plainly what they do not know, and hand off to a human instead of guessing. We test them adversarially before launch, including the awkward questions a competitor would ask.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does it cost to run?',
    a: 'Usually less than people expect. A site assistant answering a few hundred conversations a month costs single digit dollars in model usage, on top of the build. Voice costs more per minute than text. We size the model to the job rather than reaching for the most expensive one out of habit.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need a technical person to keep it running?',
    a: 'No. Once it is live the thing you maintain is the knowledge base, which is plain writing about your own business. We handle the model, the plumbing, and the updates when providers change something.',
  },
];

const breadcrumb = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://ka-performancefl.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Services', item: 'https://ka-performancefl.com/services/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'AI integration', item: PAGE_URL },
  ],
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};

const siblings = [
  {
    href: '/services/web-design/',
    kicker: 'Web design',
    blurb: 'The site the assistant lives on. Built from scratch, fast, and yours.',
  },
  {
    href: '/services/seo-ai-search/',
    kicker: 'SEO & AI search',
    blurb: 'Being the answer an assistant gives is the other half of this work.',
  },
  {
    href: '/services/accessibility/',
    kicker: 'Accessibility',
    blurb: 'Chat widgets are where accessibility usually breaks. Ours are keyboard and screen reader tested.',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="AI Integration Services for Business | K & A Performance"
  description="AI integration services from a Florida studio: site assistants that qualify leads, automations that save hours, and AI built into the product itself."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumb)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pt-40 pb-16 md:pt-48">
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-muted">
      <a href="/services/" class="transition-colors hover:text-accent">Services</a>
      <span class="text-accent" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> AI integration
    </p>
    <h1 data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.1" class="mt-6 font-display text-[clamp(2.25rem,6vw,4.5rem)] leading-[1.04]">
      AI integration services that <span class="text-accent">earn their place</span>
    </h1>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.2" class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Most AI on the web is a chat bubble bolted to a homepage so somebody
      could say the word in a meeting. We build the other kind: assistants
      that answer real questions, automations that hand hours back, and AI
      sitting inside the product where the customer never thinks about it.
      If it does not pull its weight, it does not ship.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl border-t border-ink/10 px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">Assistants that answer</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Kai, the assistant on this site, is the demo. It answers questions
      about what we do in text or out loud, it knows the actual contents of
      this business rather than a generic script, and when a conversation is
      really a lead it collects the details and passes them to a human.
      You can try both versions on the
      <a href="/services/" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-hot">services hub</a>
      before you decide whether you want one.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Yours would work the same way and sound nothing like ours. We write a
      knowledge base from your services, your pricing logic, your policies
      and your edge cases, give the assistant your voice, and set hard limits
      on what it is allowed to claim. It runs on Claude, and the whole thing
      sits on your own site rather than in a third party widget farm that
      rents your conversations back to you.
    </p>

    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-16 font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">Automations that give hours back</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      The best AI work is usually invisible. Intake forms that summarise
      themselves before they reach an inbox. Enquiries sorted and routed by
      what they are actually about. Quotes drafted from a conversation.
      Reports that write their own first paragraph. None of it is glamorous,
      and all of it is time somebody on your team currently spends retyping
      what they already know.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      We also build AI audio and content tooling: voice agents that can take
      a call and book it, and drafting tools that keep a content pipeline
      full without turning your brand into beige filler.
    </p>

    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-16 font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">When AI is the product</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <a href="https://fixalways.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-hot">fixalways.com</a>
      is the case study. It is a Florida home services directory where search
      is the whole product: a visitor describes a problem in their own words,
      including the vague ones, and the site works out what kind of pro that
      is, pulls live business data, and returns people who can actually help.
      Google Places supplies the facts, Claude supplies the understanding,
      and the visitor never sees a chat window at all.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      That is the shape we look for. Not a feature announcing itself, but a
      thing the site could not do before.
    </p>

    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-16 font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">When we say no</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Plenty of businesses ask for AI and need a faster site, clearer copy,
      or a booking flow that works on a phone. We will say so. We would
      rather build you the thing that makes money than the thing that is easy
      to sell, and we only recommend work that pays for itself in added
      value. Quotes are free either way.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl border-t border-ink/10 px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="text-center font-mono text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted">Straight answers</h2>
    <div data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.1" class="mt-6">
      {faqs.map((f) => (
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>{f.q}</summary>
          <p>{f.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-ink/10 px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl">The rest of what we do</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
      {siblings.map((s) => (
        <a href={s.href} data-animate="frame-lift" class="glow-frame group flex flex-col p-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-accent">{s.kicker}</p>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">{s.blurb}</p>
          <p class="mt-5 font-heading text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-accent">
            Read more <span class="inline-block transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 pb-40 pt-16 md:pt-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
      <p data-animate="type-settle" class="font-display text-[clamp(2.25rem,5.5vw,4.5rem)] leading-[1.05]">
        What does your team keep <span class="text-accent">repeating?</span>
      </p>
      <p data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.1" class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        That question usually finds the first thing worth automating. Tell us
        the answer and we will tell you whether AI is the right tool, and
        what it would take.
      </p>
      <div data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.2" class="mt-10">
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn-accent">Start a project</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
